      "meaning": "People speak of tradition in kindling the lamp. It is not necessarily a matter of saying “there is no such tradition”; elders may have discontinued it for some reason. One tradition is to keep the uninterrupted lamp burning through all nine days. Another is to kindle it for only five days. Or begin with Mūla nakṣatra, then Pūrvāṣāḍhā and Uttarāṣāḍhā—three days—and perform the conclusion on Śravaṇa nakṣatra. Thus the uninterrupted lamp is kindled in the final three days for the family deity. Likewise there are matters such as kindling a flour lamp daily during Navarātri. So today we… [the sentence transitions to the next video].",
