          "english": "In the next video we are giving the establishment of the uninterrupted lamp and the saṅkalpa to make for it. First, most importantly, a large lamp is needed. It can be earthen or brass. In our home there is a silver one [the following caption phrase about ācārya and silver is unclear]. You may use silver, or gold if there is gold. A good wick, a wick that stands and burns: watch it from time to time and continue adding oil or ghee. It should remain for nine days without a break. What does akhaṇḍa mean? Uninterrupted: it should remain for nine days without a break. You may kindle the lamp with a prayer that our family deity protect us in the form of light. When we receive the family deity’s blessings through the elders, our life becomes Dīpāvali, a row of lamps; it gives happiness. These are the explanations of the festivals the elders have given us.",
