          "english": "Before the lamp, complete sandhyāvandana and the worship of the deity. During all nine days perform deity worship daily. Whatever your family deity is: if Veṅkaṭeśa, recite Veṅkaṭeśa Stotra; if Narasiṃha, Narasiṃha Stuti or Narasiṃha Aṣṭottara. Or if you say, “For us it is Nañjanagūḍu Nañjuṇḍeśvara,” then the stotra of Nañjuṇḍeśvara. Some have goddesses such as Yellamma: recite the praises of that goddess, Durgā praises, daily. Worship in the morning; sit in the evening and perform recitations. Sing songs, Lakṣmī Śobhāne. Those who are able may call a nearby ācārya and have Lakṣmī Hṛdaya recitation [recovered by both GPT passes], Śrī Sūkta recitation and other recitations performed. When these are done, auspiciousness fills the home; the home’s “vibration” is good. Think of Navarātri as putting right, once a year, the changed atmosphere of the home.",
