          "english": "The vessel in which the lamp is kindled—the lamp: Sūrya and Candra are there, serving Bhagavān. Apply turmeric [native caption aśna is unclear] and kuṅkuma to the lamp vessel and decorate it with flowers. Place it on rice or on a plate [rice-or-plate wording independently supported by the targeted acoustic witness]. Some homes have a tradition of placing the lamp on gomaya, that is, cow dung. Fill it with ghee or good oil, sesame oil; put in a good wick and have it ready.",
